<title>CANADA: Canada board to hear Starbucks union bid.</title>
<headline>Canada board to hear Starbucks union bid.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British Columbia Labor Relations Board said on Monday that it will hear an application by employees of Starbucks Corp to unionize two more of its Vancouver-area stores.</p>
<p>Board spokesman Clive Lytle said the application for union certification will be heard on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, employees at three Vancouver-area outlets became the first Starbucks stores to win the right to unionize.</p>
<p>The Seattle-based company employs about 15,000 people at 970 stores across North America. Stores in the U.S. have not been organized by unions.</p>
</text>
